  "vendor_website": "www.kva.com.br",
  "description": "Automatic control and protection module for a single generator set (mains failure start), RS-485 and RS-232 Modbus RTU",
  "revision": 1,
  "revised": "2026-11-13",
  "source": "KVA, K30Plus Manual de instalação e operação, version 1.01, rev. 03, appendix B (Protocolo modbus)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "K30Plus Manual de instalação e operação",
      "version": "1.01 (rev. 03)",
      "url": "https://github.com/nobrega8/mbmap-library/issues/399",
      "note": "Appendix B, pages 57 to 61; the PDF is attached to the map request"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU with functions 0x03, 0x06 and 0x10. Serial settings: 9600 or 19200 bit/s, no, odd or even parity, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit; up to 247 modules. Factory settings: address 1, 19200 N 8 1 on both RS-485 and RS-232.",
    "The addresses are the register numbers printed in the manual (00001 to 00448). The manual does not say whether the frames use these numbers or the number minus one; the map treats them as 1-based (address_base 1). If every value looks shifted by one register, change address_base to 0.",
    "Registers marked RESERVADO in the manual (1 and 45 to 58) are left out. Register 44 holds the accumulated starts and the running time in seconds is a 32-bit value in registers 42 and 43; the manual does not state their word order (most significant register first is assumed).",
    "The manual does not give the unit or scale of the phase currents, the power factors and the remaining cooling time, nor the coding of the configuration registers 446 to 448.",
    "The keyboard command register is printed as 30008 while all other registers are numbered 00001 to 00448; it is listed at the printed number.",
    "The submitter did not confirm that the manual is public. It is the printed installation manual of a commercial product. Not tested on a device."
  ],
